  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find $a\\cdot (c\\times b)$, if $-3a\\cdot ((-2b)\\times (7c))=168.$\n\n$a\\cdot (c\\times b)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a\\cdot ((-2b)\\times (7c)) & =168 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 7\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =168 \\\\ 42[a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =168 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $b$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (c\\times b)\\,=\\,-4.\n$$",
